workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/tasks/T-069-promote-adjudicated-observations.md:88:6. **Never type a phrase.** Every form comes from an observation's `surface_form` through the observation route; no `--alias` is written by hand (OR-17: "It is not acceptable for the model to generate its own phrases/names/aliases").
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/tasks/T-071-regrade-roots.md:76:   - **a figure the source itself marks as a code's** ("Code (required)", "as required by the building code"; added 2026-11-13 by the fold of the Edmonton case study, ADJUDICATION P2): this is the source's own root attribution, not a property of the figure. Root it to the code's `ref_id` with `committee_assertion` when the code is held; else leave or set `untraced`, and say in the `--reason` the words of the marking and that the code is not held (`root_classification_basis` is not amendable: `grep -n -A3 '_AMENDABLE_SVE_FIELDS = ' scripts/db.py`; a figure written after T-035 carries the sentence there instead). Either way it supplies no independent root (OR-19). The source's own pairing of a higher figure with that code figure is an `extraction_relations` edge (`relate-extraction`), written in this batch only where both rows exist and the edge is missing; never a label, and no figure is recorded as "best practice".
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/tasks/T-082-comparator-on-two-stored-figures.md:58:**Output on 2026-11-13:** `claims with no comparator [189, 190]`; both from `REF-00992` (Approved Document M, Volume 2, UK), parameter 4, `1800 mm` "A surface width of 1800mm can accommodate any amount of non-vehicular traffic without the need for passing places." and `1200 mm` "A surface width of 1200mm may be acceptable on restricted sites, subject to agreement with the building control body." (locator section `1`, paragraph `1.11` for both); `live determinations using them 0`. No `extraction_relations` row names either (`select * from extraction_relations where from_extraction_id in (189,190) or to_extraction_id in (189,190)` printed `[]`). (Six other numerical rows with no comparator are `figure_role = 'finding'`, not claims; T-016's rule does not ask a comparator of them, and they are not this task's.)
workplan/2026-11-12-bidirectional-pipeline/tasks/T-087-edmonton-checklist-batch.md:77:5. **Figures, comparators, roles, roots and edges** (F2, F6, F7, F3; R8; P2). `=` only where the source states an exact value; a "should be", "preferred" or "recommended" figure is the bound the source's framing gives, with the warrant in the row. A threshold that triggers a rule is a `condition` row joined by `condition_on`. A figure the source itself marks as the code's ("Code (required)") is root attribution: `--root-type untraced` with `--root-classification-basis` quoting the marking, the code not being held (precedent: `select extraction_id, root_type, substr(root_classification_basis,1,60) from source_value_extractions where extraction_id in (57,64)`); it supplies no independent root (OR-19). A figure the source marks "Best Practice" is `committee_assertion` with the basis the second critic's F12 gives (not "the committee's own"). **The source's own pairing of a higher figure it recommends with the floor beside it has no relation kind** (`select sql from sqlite_master where name='extraction_relations'`: `exceeds` means the referent is more than needed, the reverse of the source; `delta_over` is an increment; `confirms` an independent measurement): write **no** edge for it, never `exceeds`; park each pairing in the same file as a `kind: "pairing"` line, the `relate-extraction` argv with the relation left as a marked hole and `waits_on: "no relation kind states a recommended figure beside a stated floor"`, and keep the SW gap naming the missing kind (OI-57 (32)). The page-1 inadequacy statement is a `figure_role='finding'` row with `--harm-finding` and its `insufficient` edge (the skill's R7 paragraph); a harm tied to no parameter is a search flag plus a gap. No stored "best practice" on any row (the owner's Q1; `grep -n -F 'best practice = the best way to do something' references/project-standards.md`).
